-- Owned, synchronized instruments. Bounds must be strictly ascending.
public define meter as opaque.
-- Kinds are "counter", "gauge", and "histogram". Only histograms use bounds.
public use "metric" function create(name text, kind text, bounds sequence of unsigned) giving failable pointer to meter.
-- Counter and gauge increments fail on overflow.
public use "metric" function add(value pointer to meter, amount unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "metric" function set(value pointer to meter, amount unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "metric" function observe(value pointer to meter, amount unsigned) giving failable nothing.
public use "metric" function value(value pointer to meter) giving failable unsigned.
public use "metric" function count(value pointer to meter) giving failable unsigned.
public use "metric" function sum(value pointer to meter) giving failable unsigned.
-- Histogram buckets are inclusive of each bound; the last bucket is overflow.
public use "metric" function bucket(value pointer to meter, index unsigned) giving failable unsigned.
-- Returns independently owned text.
public use "metric" function name(value pointer to meter) giving failable text.
-- Returns an independently owned JSON snapshot of one instrument.
public use "metric" function export(value pointer to meter) giving failable text.
public use "metric" function close(value pointer to meter) giving failable nothing.
